#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570803} :activity/id #uuid "7d547591-39b0-5426-ba80-73a612b8f3b7" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051049 :topic/id #uuid "7d21c9de-358a-52ec-b910-f6117a085d7f" :topic/math-academy-id 1814} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570803 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570771 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "142e2e05-50df-5a66-9688-4af983efdc65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to -2}f(x)=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570163} {:answer/id #uuid "4c0ad2b8-414d-5a17-bc60-4cf1f699f2a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to -2}f(x)=\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570257} {:answer/id #uuid "87134715-3e01-5440-bb15-b1ddf77a099a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to -2}f(x)=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570360} {:answer/id #uuid "ee732d08-29d7-5135-ba9f-9b7f75226b5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to -2}f(x)=\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570542} {:answer/id #uuid "ef5f59d6-b28c-51ed-af43-017b89b043d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)=-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570544}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570542} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1720c0f-a588-5d99-8985-6683833889bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570690}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b8283679-623f-5e9d-b3dc-5a2b30321fdc" :question/math-academy-id "q-35500" :question/problem "![](images/d1/d1e5821252dd0634c6033a35247af033bcda8a96fa3733b65be52565a60ea3a6.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graph of $f(x).$ Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\,-2}f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "As $x$ approaches $-2$ from the right, the function value $f(x)$ grows to infinity, and therefore\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}f(x)=\\infty .\n$$\n\nHowever, as $x$ approaches $-2$ from the left, the function value $f(x)$ goes to $-\\infty$, and therefore\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{-}}f(x)=-\\infty .\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -2}f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "1c87e3a0-0132-57e9-9e94-d890526a21d4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570811}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570811 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570768 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e5604a8-cfd8-5832-a1f4-245805b48104" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570289} {:answer/id #uuid "8728ada0-6c3b-5791-bfb2-4d61763caa83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570361} {:answer/id #uuid "8aead3f9-d0d0-5e1d-b8cd-ae8d98f0276f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570370} {:answer/id #uuid "b4617ab1-1384-53f9-b8be-1f00c735f439" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570448} {:answer/id #uuid "cd5573bc-b47f-5f58-a252-b7d45896a9a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570480}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570448} :answer-field/id #uuid "c82e8ef4-2a15-56e8-b738-07fccda39b3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b2b0f174-efe7-5216-b895-6e427b351bde" :question/math-academy-id "q-51034" :question/problem "![](images/84/84490ed5dee30eb93ae322d0d4ca20109672a80083bf9eabb252ae49c7501036.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graph of $f(x).$ Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,5}f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "As $x$ approaches $5$ from the left, the function value $f(x)$ goes to $-\\infty$, and therefore\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}f(x)=-\\infty .\n$$\n\nHowever, the function is not defined for $x>5,$ and consequently, we cannot approach $x=5$ from the right. So we have \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{+}}f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n  \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 5}f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3ede1871-f5b8-5de6-b960-f025a0d82481" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570819}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570819 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570765 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fb17250-8291-5970-b773-fdd05189cc23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570149} {:answer/id #uuid "1294d23a-8516-5a1a-b88c-fba7659b911e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570160} {:answer/id #uuid "1afaf41d-a84c-5997-be1a-1c71f3ba65be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)=\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570177} {:answer/id #uuid "87adca47-db00-5cd0-9e1b-f73136fac8b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)=\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570364} {:answer/id #uuid "fd423fcc-7cf3-54fa-8641-192b765ae5b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)=-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570573}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570573} :answer-field/id #uuid "e026018c-c11f-523c-bb59-03bedfd7598b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570682}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a9e5a7d0-a42d-53f5-8ae1-26c9c5fee794" :question/math-academy-id "q-75543" :question/problem "![](images/cc/cc2ea14272a30271bb022e9deb5e8b506ed0c2725d6633e7308b3786cb09d84c.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graph of $f(x).$ Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "We see from the graph that as $x$ approaches $-1$ from the left, the function $f(x)$ approaches $-\\infty .$ So, the left-hand limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x)=-\\infty \\,.\n$$\n\nLikewise, as $x$ approaches $-1$ from the right, the function $f(x)$ again approaches $-\\infty .$ So, the right-hand limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}f(x)=-\\infty \\,.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)=-\\infty \\,.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "51ae2c5a-962e-5d21-8c31-b89b3b4db781" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570866}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570866 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570767 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df1eac84-5cbe-5960-af4e-3fe21f5a9174" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570516}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570516} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f9558dc-c88c-5f2c-b94c-48629251ff71" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570628}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ae5c5c63-a42c-5945-a9b3-a559880f74b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-338954" :question/problem "![](images/8c/8c0a344d98dc0ca3a6e4c0fdc3c98074bc2de23301300e663a02ea6f4dff3035.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graph of $f(x).$ Therefore\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,6}f(x)=$\n\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We see from the graph that as $x$ approaches $6$ from the left, the function $f(x)$ approaches $\\infty .$ So, the left-hand limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {6}^{-}}f(x)=\\infty \\,.\n$$\n\nLikewise, as $x$ approaches $6$ from the right, the function $f(x)$ again approaches $\\infty .$ So, the right-hand limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {6}^{+}}f(x)=\\infty \\,.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 6}f(x)=\\infty \\,.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "df01aa43-5f29-55b3-96cc-9f5e0a72a50a"}] :activity/title "Infinite Limits from Graphs" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570105}]}
